00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,500
What Does an LE-500 Rating Mean for Archival Microfilm?. A guide for archivists and records managers

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,332
An LE-500 rating (also written LE500) means archival microfilm is expected to stay usable for 500 years.

3
00:00:15,332 --> 00:00:23,084
It holds only when the film, its processing and its storage all meet the ISO standards. LE stands for life expectancy.

4
00:00:23,084 --> 00:00:26,500
It is the rating specified for preservation masters.

5
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:36,257
Condition: The film. Standard: ISO 18901. What it requires: Silver-gelatin emulsion on a polyester base. Acetate does not qualify.. Condition: The processing.

6
00:00:36,257 --> 00:00:44,792
Standard: ISO 18917. What it requires: Fixer residue below set limits, checked with the methylene blue test.. Condition: The storage. Standard: ISO 18911.

7
00:00:44,792 --> 00:00:50,500
What it requires: Cool, stable temperature, controlled humidity and clean air, in archival enclosures..

8
00:00:51,500 --> 00:01:01,937
It is not a property of the film alone: it rates film, processing and storage together. It does not apply automatically to duplicates, which carry their own ratings.

9
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:12,500
It is not a guarantee of image quality. Legibility is tested separately, against ISO 6199 resolution targets. If any one condition fails, the rating no longer applies.

10
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:23,275
1. Ask for the specification sheet: stating LE-500 to ISO 18901. 2. Require methylene blue results: to ISO 18917 for each processing batch. 3.

11
00:01:23,275 --> 00:01:32,500
State the storage conditions: to ISO 18911, or confirm the vault meets them. 4. Ask for readings: resolution and density on each roll.

12
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:42,017
Is LE500 the same as LE-500? Yes. Both spellings refer to the same 500-year rating. Does digital storage have an equivalent rating? No.

13
00:01:42,017 --> 00:01:48,453
Digital media have no comparable rating and need regular migration. How is processing quality checked?

14
00:01:48,453 --> 00:01:53,500
With the methylene blue test in ISO 18917, which measures residual thiosulphate.

